Package: CSMatch
Title: Caliper Synthetic Matching
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Xiang", "Meng", , "xmeng@g.harvard.edu", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0000-7502-1314")),
    person("Jonathan", "Che", , "jche@exponent.com", role = c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Luke", "Miratrix", , "lmiratrix@g.harvard.edu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0078-1906")))
Description: Implements Caliper Synthetic Matching (CSM), a method for
    matching in observational studies. Given treated and control units, CSM
    performs radius (caliper) matching on a user-specified covariate
    distance metric, then builds a synthetic control for each treated unit
    from its matched controls via constrained optimization. The package
    provides diagnostic tools for selecting a distance metric and caliper,
    assessing covariate balance and match quality, and estimating the
    average treatment effect on the treated together with several variance
    estimators. Methods are described in Che, Meng, and Miratrix (2024)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2411.05246>.
